WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.969 --> 00:00:06.420
Mana Onsgaard's home looks a bit like an antiques
store.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:09.920
He can't sell everything he salvages from
the river straight away.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:18.640
It's best to collect as much as possible before
looking for a buyer.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:24.520
In recent weeks he's collected amulets, coins
and glass beads.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:29.259
Mana comes home with a haul pretty much every
single day - but it doesn't always include

00:00:29.259 --> 00:00:31.980
anything of real value.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:41.680
"If I find something underwater that I think
could be gold, I bite on it.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.300
Most metals have a bitter taste, but gold
doesn't taste of anything.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.730
It's also heavy and smooth.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:53.070
A gold breastplate is the most valuable thing
I ever found.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:56.870
It was seven years ago, after the 2011 floods.

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:59.070
I got 1300 euros for it.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:03.050
I sold this ring for 800 euros.

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:08.180
That was a while ago."

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:14.240
The buyers are antiques dealers.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.580
Mana doesn't want to name them.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:23.690
He knows the whole trade in sunken treasure
is a legal grey area.

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:30.409
"Of course all these things belonged to someone,
before they ended up in the water.

00:01:30.409 --> 00:01:35.500
But as long as they aren't national relics,
you can keep them.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:38.820
I have had some encounters with the authorities.

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:45.619
But one man's trash is another man's treasure."+++
Mana lives in a house on stilts directly on

00:01:45.619 --> 00:01:47.470
the river.

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:52.630
The settlement is called Mittakam and was
built around 100 years ago.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:57.300
Mana's grandfather was one of the first inhabitants.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:02.030
Today the floating village of Mittakam is
home to about 120 people.

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:06.520
Most of the men are treasure divers like Mana.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:13.150
Mana's 11-year-old daughter goes to school
and his wife Yui works as a chambermaid in

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:14.150
a hotel.

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:18.480
She used to go out with him when he went diving
- but only as a lookout.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:22.420
Traditionally, women don't dive themselves.

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:27.840
"It isn't women's work.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:29.690
Unless you're especially brave.

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:32.850
The thought of being unerwater scares me.

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:41.060
You don't know what's there - shards of glass,
nails...My husband is an experienced diver.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:48.300
But I still worry everytime he goes diving."

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.460
Mana learnt to dive from his father.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.430
It's the only skill he has.

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:57.540
His homemade diving helmet is his most important
piece of equipment.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:04.680
It weighs over 20 kilos.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:14.050
While Prayad lays anchor, Mana gets ready
for his first dive.

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:17.630
That involves the traditional "Wai Khru" ceremony.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:30.690
Mana pays his respects to his ancestors and
asks them to protect him.

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:39.849
His partner puts the heavy helmet on his head...and
then he's off.

00:03:39.849 --> 00:03:44.209
The weight of it pushes him straight under.

00:03:44.209 --> 00:03:52.599
There's zero visibility underwater.

00:03:52.599 --> 00:04:04.050
Mana finally comes back up.

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:26.980
He shows us a handful of coins that he's found.

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:31.510
Mana's also brought up some sludge from the
riverbed, which they'll sift through in search

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:41.790
of other valuables.

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:47.960
Today's findings include a piece of fishing
sinker and a few more coins from the 19th

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:49.650
century.

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:54.020
"I'm happy enough.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:57.740
Coins like these aren't all that special,
I find quite a few of them.

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:01.120
You can get one or two hundred Baht for them.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:03.630
Obviously gold is much more valuable.

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:08.800
But gold isn't something you find every day."+++
9:12

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:15.660
Mana and Prayad spent about 6 hours on the
water today, taking it in turns to go diving.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:21.860
By the end of the day, they've recovered some
two dozen old coins.

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:26.340
They'll make about 25 euros - over three times
more than what they would have earnt in a

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:29.490
minimum wage job.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:33.770
Mana hopes he'll be able to continue making
a living as a treasure diver.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:35.860
The river is a gift that keeps on giving.

